{
  "duration": 88.659,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.079,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.559,
      "end": 2.539,
      "text": "It's time to solve"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.079,
      "end": 3.839,
      "text": "one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.259,
      "end": 5.339,
      "text": "Now, in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.859,
      "end": 6.579,
      "text": "we are given that"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.079,
      "end": 7.739,
      "text": "cos theta"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.319,
      "end": 10.059,
      "text": "is equal to four by five."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.539,
      "end": 12.399,
      "text": "Also, theta is an acute angle."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.92,
      "end": 14.899,
      "text": "The problem is asking us to find sine theta."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.779,
      "end": 21.039,
      "text": "Now, before we start solving, let us first understand what this given value is telling us."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.359,
      "end": 25.059,
      "text": "We know that cos theta is equal to adjacent upon hypotenuse."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.5,
      "end": 27.399,
      "text": "So when cos theta is four by five,"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.819,
      "end": 29.099,
      "text": "we are sure about one fact,"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.619,
      "end": 34.779,
      "text": "the adjacent side is four units and the hypotenuse is five units."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.54,
      "end": 37.54,
      "text": "So let us find the opposite side first."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.239,
      "end": 40.159,
      "text": "Here we will use the Pythagoras Theorem."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.86,
      "end": 44.939,
      "text": "Hypotenuse square is equal to adjacent square plus opposite square."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.599,
      "end": 47.339,
      "text": "Now substitute the known values."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.0,
      "end": 51.139,
      "text": "Five square is equal to four square plus opposite square."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.719,
      "end": 52.619,
      "text": "After solving this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 53.259,
      "end": 56.159,
      "text": "the opposite side becomes three units."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.899,
      "end": 57.319,
      "text": "Got it?"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.02,
      "end": 58.499,
      "text": "Perfect."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.239,
      "end": 61.099,
      "text": "Now we know all three sides of the triangle."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.779,
      "end": 64.18,
      "text": "So let us check the formula for sine."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.879,
      "end": 69.04,
      "text": "Sine theta is equal to opposite upon hypotenuse."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.72,
      "end": 71.059,
      "text": "Now substitute the values."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.739,
      "end": 74.119,
      "text": "This becomes three upon five."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.68,
      "end": 79.58,
      "text": "Also, the question clearly says that theta is an acute angle,"
    },
    {
      "start": 80.279,
      "end": 82.239,
      "text": "so sine theta will be positive."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.68,
      "end": 83.099,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 83.659,
      "end": 85.719,
      "text": "the final answer will be three by five."
    },
    {
      "start": 86.18,
      "end": 86.599,
      "text": "Therefore,"
    },
    {
      "start": 87.199,
      "end": 88.659,
      "text": "option B is the correct answer."
    }
